# Android client

Native Kotlin/Jetpack Compose shell for `{{ project_title }}`, generated by the
cliver-playbook scaffold. The project owns these files; edit them freely.

## Layout

| Module | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `app` | Single activity, theme, adaptive navigation shell and home screen. |
| `contracts` | Generated Kotlin wire client (Gson, coroutines); do not edit by hand. |
| `core` | HTTP client over the generated APIs, model aliases, secure token storage, auth state, theme and window-size helpers. |
| `feature/auth` | Sign-in and registration (only when the auth feature is enabled). |
| `feature/profile` | Profile view and edit (only when the profile feature is enabled). |
| `feature/products` | Reference product list, detail, create, edit and delete screens (only when the CRUD feature is enabled). |

A disabled feature is not included in `settings.gradle.kts` and the app module
does not depend on it. The generated source tree is the manifest's decision;
change `project-manifest.yaml` and re-run the scaffolder to add or remove a
feature.

`feature/products` is a reference slice, not domain code. Replace or delete it
when the project has its own entities.

## Generated API client

`contracts` is generated from `contracts/openapi.yaml` with OpenAPI Generator
(`kotlin`, `jvm-okhttp4`, Gson, coroutines, Java 8 dates). `core` aliases the
generated models as `User`, `AuthSession`, `Product` and friends; its
`ApiClient` calls the generated `AuthApi`, `ProductsApi` and `AgentApi`. The
SSE stream stays a small custom OkHttp transport because OpenAPI does not
model server-sent events.

Do not edit `contracts/src/main/kotlin` by hand. After changing a contract
fragment:

```sh
./scripts/generate-contracts.sh          # from apps/android
```

`scripts/generate-contracts.sh --check` verifies the recorded contract hash;
`--verify` regenerates in a temporary directory and diffs the result. Both
need Node and Java 17+. Generation is also wired to `make contracts` and
`make contracts-verify-native` at the project root.

## Requirements

JDK 17, Android SDK Platform 35, Build-Tools 35.0.0 and Android Studio. The
Gradle 8.10.2 wrapper is checked in, so a separate Gradle installation is not
required. The versions in the build files are the scaffold's defaults; a
project may bump them together with AGP. Newer platforms (for example API 37)
can stay installed, but AGP 8.8 still needs Platform 35 and Build-Tools 35.0.0
for this project's `compileSdk = 35`.

## Optional static check

`ktlint` is optional; `.editorconfig` configures the Android code style and
lets `@Composable` entry points keep PascalCase. The authoritative gate is
still the Gradle build:

```sh
ktlint "**/*.kt"
./gradlew :app:assembleDebug test
```

## Gradle wrapper

The Gradle 8.10.2 wrapper is checked in and matches Android Gradle Plugin
8.8.0, so the project builds without a machine-wide Gradle installation:

```sh
./gradlew :app:assembleDebug test
```

Android Studio can also sync the project and use the same wrapper.

## API base URL

`BuildConfig.API_BASE_URL` defaults to `http://10.0.2.2:8000/api/v1`, the
emulator's route to the host loopback. Override it without editing code:

```sh
./gradlew :app:assembleDebug -PapiBaseUrl=<your-api-base-url>
```

Cleartext HTTP is allowed only for `10.0.2.2`, `127.0.0.1` and `localhost`
(`app/src/main/res/xml/network_security_config.xml`). A physical device needs
an HTTPS endpoint, or its own explicit network security exemption.

## UI seam

`core/.../ui/AppComponents.kt` defines the visual slots (`productCard`,
`emptyState`, `primaryButton`, `chatMessage`, `composer`, `toolCall`) and the
`LocalAppComponents` composition local. `PlaybookTheme` provides the reference
implementation by default; a project replaces a slot at its `PlaybookTheme`
call (or overrides the local deeper in the tree) without editing feature state
or data flow. The product list already reads its card and empty state through
this seam.

## Assistant

When the agent feature is enabled, the first destination is the Assistant tab.
`ChatScreen` posts to `/agent/runs`, consumes the SSE stream through
`ApiClient.streamAgentRun`, and renders messages and tool calls through
`LocalAppComponents`. A products selection exposes an "Open products" action;
the Home, products and profile destinations remain available.

## Adaptive navigation

`NavigationSuiteScaffold` switches automatically with the window width from
`currentWindowAdaptiveInfo()` (see `core/.../ui/Adaptive.kt`):

| Width | Navigation |
|---|---|
| Compact (phones) | Bottom navigation bar |
| Medium (small tablets, foldables) | Navigation rail |
| Expanded (tablets, desktop-size windows) | Navigation drawer |

The product list uses a `LazyColumn` on compact widths and a responsive
`LazyVerticalGrid` on wider ones. The theme follows the system dark mode and
Material You dynamic colour when available.

## Session storage

Bearer tokens are stored in `EncryptedSharedPreferences` backed by the Android
Keystore (`core/.../auth/TokenStore.kt`). A 401 response clears the token and
returns the app to sign-in.

## Namespace

The generated namespace and application id are `com.example.android`. Rename
them and the matching package directories before publishing to a store; a
release build cannot be shipped under the shared example id.
